set up for the win, not having mathed out the attacks of existing constructs to realize that the last Hellion would turn Nigel into Reaper chow.  \n\nOh well, at least now I've experienced just what the \"Overcome by Manifestations\" side of him does (and what it looks like by default, since I've previously only seen the promo version).  Not a huge fan overall, as he rivals Spite for how boring the fight is (but is far less frustrating, without the armor and the \"unplaying\" of cards), but in this case a well-timed Oppressive Smog made it a good bit more manageable.  Two rounds of Thorathian Monolith bought me the time to set Argent up the rest of the way, and with every Mannie only healing him for 2 instead of 4, CC and SS were able to make pretty short work of him.",
